# The lines the Slang twin of water/main.frag may declare differently from the GLSL (task 0072, water family), read by
# SlangPermutations in components-tests: "[<define set>] glsl-only: <line>"; every listed line must occur, so a stale
# entry fails the test. All of them are declarations the GLSL keeps and never reads (glslang keeps unused
# declarations, Slang drops them); a pipeline layout may hold bindings and a vertex stage may write outputs a shader
# does not read, so nothing the pipeline builds changes.
#
# For every set:
# - bindings 14 and 15, the volumetric fog's image and parameters (lib/view/volume.glsl through lib/view/fog.glsl): the
#   water calls applyFog(colour, distance), which never reads the volume;
# - input location 1, pointLightDiffuse of lib/inout.glsl: the water's fragment stage never reads it.
# With CLOUD_SHADOW_DEBUG, also bindings 6 and 7, the shadow map and its sampler: shadow() then returns the clouds'
# shadow alone and never samples the shadow maps.
